{
 "id": "IgProfilePosts01",
 "name": "Pull the latest posts and reels from Instagram profiles to Google Sheets with Apify",
 "active": false,
 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "sticky-main",
   "name": "Overview",
   "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
   "typeVersion": 1,
   "position": [
    -980,
    -300
   ],
   "parameters": {
    "width": 700,
    "height": 820,
    "content": "# Pull the latest posts and reels from Instagram profiles to Google Sheets with Apify\n\nGive it Instagram handles or profile URLs and get each profile's latest posts and reels as a spreadsheet: caption, hashtags, like and comment counts, plays and duration for videos, the media URL and the permalink, one row per post, newest by date.\n\n### Who it's for\nSocial teams, researchers and agencies who track what a set of public profiles is posting, without an Instagram login and without a page size deciding how many rows they pay for.\n\n### How it works\n1. A Set node holds the profiles, how many posts to fetch per profile, and an optional post-type filter.\n2. An HTTP Request runs the Instagram Profile Posts Scraper on Apify. The limit is exact (30 means 30), pinned posts are flagged rather than promoted, and posts it could not deliver are uncharged.\n3. An If node keeps the post rows (the profile and summary rows are dropped), a Set node tidies the columns and a Google Sheets node appends them.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create an HTTP Header Auth credential (name `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`) and select it on the HTTP Request node.\n2. Connect Google Sheets and pick the spreadsheet and sheet.\n3. Open the Config node, set the profiles (comma-separated handles or URLs) and the posts per profile; optionally set `mediaType` to `image`, `video` or `carousel`.\n4. Run the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\nAn Apify account and a Google account. Two profiles × 30 posts is about $0.15 on the free plan; from 16 September 2026 each profile that delivers posts adds one $0.003 profile lookup (about $0.006 more for two), and a profile that delivers nothing pays none.\n\n### Customization tips\nChain the run's dataset into the Instagram Reel Transcript Scraper to turn the video posts into transcripts. Add a Schedule Trigger and the actor's watchlist fields (`watchlistId`, `newPostsOnly`) to pay only for new posts on each run.\n"
   }
  },
